<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kara Mustafa Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1634–<a href="/years/1683">1683</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kara Mustafa Pasha was an Ottoman grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the late seventeenth century. He led the Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1683, which was broken by a relief army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-iii-sobieski">Jan III Sobieski</a>. The defeat led to his execution and began a long series of Ottoman territorial losses in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kara-mustafa-pasha.jpg" alt="Kara Mustafa Pasha" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksmuseum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_Kara_Mustafa_Pasha,_RP-P-1894-A-18289.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
